## FENCES, PARTITION, HOLDS
- **Git:** root history writes only `worktree add -b`, ONE commit and ONE `merge --no-ff`. No `worktree remove`, `fetch`, `push`, `stash`, `reset`, `rebase`, `amend`, `prune`, `gc`, `clean`, `checkout`, no fast-forward of any other branch. In the code repository: `gh api -X GET` only; you clone nothing and edit no file there.
- **HTTP:** `gh api -X GET` to the code repository; the Jira site named in the project's `.env` for GETs, the one comment POST, the up-to-one transition POST and the up-to-one create POST (python `-I -B`, credentials in-process, never printed). No mailbox, no demo, no hosted or production host, no package or container registry. No az, ssh, docker, npm, node, tests, build, deploy, mail, chat, Artifact, Docs, pull request, merge of any pull request, card or `decision_queue.sh`; no message to any human; no comment or edit on any pull request.
- **Partition, from this side:** yours are root `main` (the one merge), `.tools/wt-b2007-rec`, `records/b2007`; your Step-0 copy, STATUS, `Briefs/2026-11-23_B2007_evidence/`, `.tools/b2007/`; the Jira writes of the closed list. **Read-only:** the two review folders in Tuesday's `briefs/`, the B1959 STATUS and evidence, the B1957 STATUS, `.tools/b1957/scripts/`, `.tools/b1509/scripts/`, `.tools/b1808/scripts/`. **Not yours:** every Jira key but PCOMP-67 and the one new Task, `2_Project_Files` code, every other seat's tree, the stale README of any directory, PCOMP-31 to PCOMP-36 and PCOMP-66. **From the other side:** the OXPd records seat and the NexusAI records seat (other projects) write their own projects only; no Composer pane is known at drafting (`tmux list-panes -a` printed the coordinator's pane, the two named seats above and unnamed panes at 20:50:51; the seat re-reads).
- **Standing lines:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (above); no message to any human; Jira writes: only the closed list, only under the slots; never delete (quarantine); never print a credential; no word added to any user-facing text; `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a red you cannot explain is a STOP; a check of this kit whose line says STOP and that fails ends the run `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` even when you can explain the cause.
- **HOLDS:** no deploy and no statement about the hosted state (what the demo runs is NOT known and no text says); the product owner's standing hold binds: no text says or implies a deploy of a changed content release is due, approved, scheduled or done; no ruling of your own; no label edit on any existing issue and no description edit; no edit of any code, of the README or of `DEPLOY.md`; no new lane; PCOMP-67 and the new Task are touched only as the closed list says; no comment on PCOMP-31 to PCOMP-35, PCOMP-36, PCOMP-37 or PCOMP-66; no word of the template, the sample or the vendor in any text.

